 R←Test_10(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;rc;more;wsname;folder;fno;crash
⍝ Fires up a runtime instance (Test_WS_3.DWS) that has a thread running when the error occurs:
⍝ `Process` must kill the thread and still save an error WS. This cannot be done in the development
⍝ session: killing all threads would kill the session's own threads (Link, Cider, Tatin...) as well.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 wsname←FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath ##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/Tests/Test_WS_3.DWS'
 folder←FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath ##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/Tests/Errors_WS_3'     ⍝ As defined in Test_WS_3.DWS
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir folder

 (rc more)←GetResultFromSecondDyalogInstance wsname
 →T.GoToTidyUp 124≠rc                                          ⍝ `returnCode` as defined in Test_WS_3.DWS
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢FilesAndDirs.ListFiles folder,'/*.dws'       ⍝ The error WS got saved...
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢FilesAndDirs.ListFiles folder,'/*.dcf'
 fno←(⊃FilesAndDirs.ListFiles folder,'/*.dcf')⎕FTIE 0
 crash←⎕FREAD fno 1
 ⎕FUNTIE fno
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0 1≢crash.TNUMS                                ⍝ The thread was running when the error occurred...
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠crash.⎕NC'SaveFailed'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢FilesAndDirs.ListFiles folder,'/*.html'
 →T.GoToTidyUp(,'0')≢⊃⊃⎕NGET(folder,'/TNUMS.txt')1            ⍝ ...and the thread is gone (written by `customFns`)
 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir folder
